    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Cal Raleigh** stands as our premier offensive anchor with a score of 61.37. While Shane Baz presents a moderate test, **Cal Raleigh** benefits from a high-leverage spot at #2 in the order and a park factor that aligns well with his profile. Close behind, **Matt Chapman** (59.09) and **Luis Arraez** (58.53) are the primary drivers of our production against Mart\u00edn P\u00e9rez. Both benefit significantly from favorable wind conditions and the relative softness of P\u00e9rez\u2019s xERA, allowing **Matt Chapman** to leverage his position in the heart of the order, while **Luis Arraez** maintains his value floor through high-contact efficiency despite the platoon disadvantage.\n\nThe optimizer faced a difficult decision at the bottom of the order, ultimately favoring **Drew Gilbert** (44.12) over **Jeremiah Jackson** (38.92). While **Drew Gilbert** deals with a L/L platoon hurdle against P\u00e9rez, his projected floor held steadier than that of **Jeremiah Jackson**, who struggled to overcome the SP skill penalty posed by Bryan Woo. Elsewhere, we are cautious with **Bryson Stott** (42.71) and **Taylor Ward** (43.69); both players are battling unfavorable matchups against Sean Manaea and Bryan Woo respectively, coupled with negative platoon adjustments. While they remain in the starting lineup for now, their utility is strictly marginal, and we will be monitoring their confirmed batting orders closely to ensure they don't slide further down into positions that would suppress their counting stat potential.\n\nNote that all scoring is currently predicated on \"Lineup Pending\" assumptions. Should **Cal Raleigh**, **Luis Arraez**, or any other core starter be dropped significantly in the order once official lineups are posted, we will re-evaluate the risk of burning game caps. We are also monitoring the status of **Will Smith** and **Daulton Varsho** on the IL, whose absences continue to limit our flexibility at the catcher and outfield slots, placing additional pressure on the production of **Masyn Winn** and **Jung Hoo Lee** to maintain our SB pacing.",
